# Design qualities

## Componentization

Small cohesive components (slices, adapters, ports) with clear ownership and small public surface. Prefer compose-over-invent. Align with modules; no shared domain dumping ground.

## DRY with judgment

- Deduplicate technical primitives (resilience, telemetry, problem codes, Options).
- Do not share product domain across modules via “convenient” base types.
- Rule of three / wrong abstraction: copy-adapt beats premature shared domain.
- Delete pass-through wrappers and dead parallel implementations when touched.

## Maintainability

Feature folders match business language. One change ≈ one vertical slice. Document only hard-to-recover decisions (ADR/feature SDD).

## Extensibility

Add handler/strategy/adapter/slice — not boolean flags in shared code. Contracts evolve additively within v1.

## Scalability

Stay modular monolith until independent scale, failure isolation, data ownership, release cadence, or compliance forces a split. Measure before caching/sharding.
